abstract: >-
  Adversarial cross-emitter test vectors for JSON canonicalization schemes,
  covering ten Wycheproof-style categories: unicode-normalization,
  lone-surrogate, deep-nesting, integer-edge, empty-structure,
  mixed-type-array, sort-collision, zwj-rtl, escaped-control, and
  boolean-integer-overlap. Designed to surface byte-level divergences
  across the ten official Model Context Protocol SDK implementations
  (TypeScript, Python, Go, Swift, Java, Kotlin, C#, PHP, Ruby, Rust) and
  by extension across any JSON parser or canonicalizer that consumes them.
